  "lineage": "Iranian classical system organized as the radif, a canonical body of some 250 gusheh melodic models distributed across seven dastgah and five avaz, assembled and taught in Qajar Tehran by Mirza Abdollah and Aqa Hoseinqoli around 1900 — an unmetred avaz section in which a solo voice and tar or santur trade phrases in strict heterophony, punctuated by metered tasnif songs and fast chaharmezrab etudes over tombak goblet-drum patterns.",
